        "text": "That was a great talk and very inspiring. The tight linking of apps and their canvas representation puts me off investing in layout algorithms because they seem so complex and limited in scope to the application they were develop for, which often does not justify the cost of developing them. My mind has been racing since about meta-layout algorithms that layout _any_ diagram by _any_ tool which makes more economic sense to me.\n\nNow I wonder if you can take an ocwg diagram, convert to graphviz, let graphviz do the layout and then export out again :thinking_face:",
